{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Aromatic spices, by the head.</b> An expression of counting, as in 'כי תשא את ראש בני ישראל' — meaning that one takes them according to the count that he tallies. And since above it said 'aromatic spices for the anointing oil' and did not specify what they are and their amounts, now it specifies for you." "<b>Aromatic spices.</b> They are types of tree exudates, as it is written 'הפיחי גני יזלו בשמיו'. But 'סמים' are types of sap and not roots that grow in the ground."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:16.857253879Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}